canon evidence add: BRIEF_UNAPPROVED — unreviewed-promotion checkout — evidence for c-checkout#1: brief not approved — .canon/changes/c-checkout/brief.md has no `Approved:` line, so the human has not answered it; when they answer, the human records it with `canon brief approve c-checkout --approver <their name> --note "<their words>"` in their own shell (or on `canon dashboard`); never run it yourself or unset your role to run it
hint: stop, report the brief to the human and wait for their answer: nothing is built or attested for a subject before its brief is approved. The human records their answer in their own shell (`canon brief approve --approver <their name> --note "<their words>"`, or on `canon dashboard`); never run it yourself or unset your role to run it; to attest anyway, pass --override-reason <text>, which is recorded on the evidence record
